# bb_rt.py — raytraced breakaway (Ballblazer-inspired), milestone 6 (GENERATED by gen_rt.py — edit the generator)
# rt_main(): asm, core 1, never returns until CTRL[EXIT]: game logic, per-frame setup, even rows.
# rt_rows(): asm, called by io_loop on core 0 each frame: odd rows, then returns.
# io_loop(): Viper on core 0 — gamepad -> CTRL, rt_rows, 2x doubling, HUD.
#
# Scene: mode-7 floor with box-filtered checker, Fresnel floor reflections (objects
# mirrored through the floor plane), soft contact shadow, emissive orb with glow and
# floor light, three chrome defenders (ellipsoids) with one reflection bounce, rim and
# stripe, emissive goal posts, analytic edge anti-aliasing. Sky: ringed gas giant and
# stars (in every reflection), translucent arena walls, collision spark bursts.
# Game: start each run carrying the orb at one end of a long field; three defenders
# guard zones and try to ram it loose. GAMEPAD_LEFT/RIGHT strafe. Shoot (GAMEPAD_UP) straight ahead into the
# sliding goal; the reticle marks your heading. A defender
# touching a loose orb is a turnover. All of it runs inside rt_main.
# Colors: PALETTES below (GAMEPAD_DOWN cycles them live).
